THIRD-PARTY DATA
----------------

cognisom/data/sections/prostate_xenium_600um.csv contains measured human
prostate cell positions derived from a 10x Genomics public dataset:

    Xenium Prime 5K FFPE Human Prostate (adenocarcinoma), 10x Genomics,
    published 2024-07-31.
    https://www.10xgenomics.com/datasets/xenium-prime-ffpe-human-prostate

    Copyright 10x Genomics. Licensed under the Creative Commons
    Attribution 4.0 International Licence (CC BY 4.0),
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

CC BY 4.0 is compatible with Apache 2.0 and governs only that file, not
the rest of this repository. The file is a transformation of the source
cells.csv.gz: one 600 um window, four columns, re-originned coordinates,
and an equivalent circular diameter computed per cell. Its own header
records the source URL, the source checksum, the selection rule and the
QC filter, so the attribution travels with the data. Anyone redistributing
that file, or a derivative of it, must keep the 10x Genomics attribution.

cognisom/genomics/su2c_prostate_demo.vcf contains the somatic callset of
one patient (sample SC_9184_T, patient 97115558) extracted from a public
prostate cancer cohort:

    Abida et al., "Genomic correlates of clinical outcome in advanced
    prostate cancer", PNAS 2019, PMID 31061129. SU2C/PCF Dream Team:
    Precision Therapy for Advanced Prostate Cancer. Obtained via
    cBioPortal study prad_su2c_2019.
    https://www.cbioportal.org/study/summary?id=prad_su2c_2019

    Licensed under the Open Data Commons Open Database License (ODbL)
    1.0, http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/

ODbL is a share-alike licence for databases and governs only that file,
not the rest of this repository. It requires that public use of the
database, or of works produced from it, be attributed; that resulting
data-sets stay open; and that a shared or adapted version be offered
under ODbL. Anyone redistributing that VCF, or a derivative of it, must
keep the SU2C/PCF attribution and the ODbL terms.

The file is a transformation of the cohort's data_mutations.txt: one
patient's 93 somatic rows, converted to VCF by scripts/su2c_to_vcf.py.
Its own header records the source study, the PMID, the licence, the
genome build, and — the part a reader most needs — that the normal
column's 0/0 genotype asserts the consortium's somatic determination
rather than carrying normal read evidence, because the source publishes
none. The cohort MAF itself is NOT redistributed here; data/ is
gitignored.
